WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.634
-Welcome, welcome back
to the show.

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:03.934
-Hi, Jimmy.
-I miss you so much.

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:05.367
-We miss you.
-I watch you all the time.

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:06.601
So I'm used to you in my life,

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:08.734
but to see you in person,
I just love seeing you.

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:10.934
And congrats.
Looking gorg on the cover

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:12.300
of "Good Housekeeping"
right there.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.868
Not too shabby.

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:15.200
-Thank you.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.067
-I wanted to ask you,

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:20.000
because I watch you, seriously,
every single morning.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.267
-Mm-hm.
-When do you get --

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:22.734
to get any time off?
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:25.300
-And do you go on vacation
when you do take time off?

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:26.901
-We just actually both --
-Yeah.

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:28.367
-I took a whole spring break.
-Yes.

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:29.968
-My first spring break
I've ever taken

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.667
because both kids
were on the same schedule.

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:32.968
So we took the kids.

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:35.934
I basically -- The last time
I took my little boy

00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:38.067
on an airplane ride, he was 3.

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:39.467
It was horrible.

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.334
He was, like, basically
crawling under seats

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:43.634
and was like a foot rest
for the other passengers.

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:45.834
So I put him on a no-fly list.

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:48.501
-Yeah. It's good
that the parents do it.

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:50.167
-And, like, literally,
three years passed,

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:51.701
and I'm like,
"Let's give you a chance.

00:00:51.701 --> 00:00:52.734
You're on probation."

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:54.400
So, we went
and we had best time.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.601
He learned to swim.
-See? That's fantastic.

00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:57.801
-Come on.
-I know.

00:00:57.801 --> 00:00:59.367
So he's potty trained.
He learned to swim.

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:01.801
I'm like -- Drop the mic.
I'm done. It's over.

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:03.667
-Also, I should say,
he's 17 years old.

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:04.968
But that's amazing.
-It's awkward.

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:06.667
-Potty training comes
when it comes.

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:08.234
-But they always say, like,
"Your kid won't go off

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:09.567
to college with diapers."

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:11.501
I'm like, "Well, if it happens."
-This one might, yeah.

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:13.000
This one might.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.901
I saw Jenna Bush Hager
was talking --

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:17.734
talking about this vacation.

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:20.534
'Cause she went with you.
-She totally busted Savannah.

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:22.968
She busted you out.

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:24.300
-No, because,
apparently, this --

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.367
it was your wedding anniversary
on your vacation.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:28.267
-Turns out.
-Yeah.

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:30.901
You woke up and you had no idea
it was your anniversary?

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:32.400
-Well, what happened --

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.634
It wasn't the first thought
when I woke up.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.467
And I don't think
it was my husband's, either.

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:37.734
And we took the kids --

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.634
the Hagers and our family,
we all --

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:41.300
we took them to the water park.
-Yeah.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.734
And we're, like, on this, like,
bus to the water park.

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:45.234
And all of a sudden,
Mike's like,

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:46.634
"Is today our anniversary?"

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:50.200
And I'm like, "It is, actually!"
So it is.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.901
-How romantic.
-Oh, I know.

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.667
We were at the water park,
I know.

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:56.033
Like, yeah, getting
waterborne illnesses.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:58.968
-And how are the girls?
-Oh, my God.

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:00.367
Haley -- I've got -- You guys,

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:02.767
I have a 5-year-old
and a 3-year-old now.

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:04.434
They -- Can you believe
that they're that old?

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:05.834
-No, I can't believe
they're 5 and 3.

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:08.667
-I know. They both
recently had birthdays.

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:10.400
-And do you go all-out,
Hoda Kotb?

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.367
-No, let me tell you what I do.

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:15.667
I do something y'all should do,
because it's super easy and fun.

00:02:15.667 --> 00:02:20.200
I make the best birthday cakes.
But let me tell you the secret.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.601
Because we have this chef
named Elizabeth Heiskell.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:24.067
-Yeah.
-She's like -- She goes,

00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:25.901
"Hoda, look.
Don't be mixing everything.

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:28.100
Just dump it in.
It's a dump cake."

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:31.567
So, what you do is you take
the Duncan Hines --

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:34.934
Dump it in. Pour the egg in.
Barely stir it.

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:37.267
Just barely.
Stick it in the oven.

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:39.167
-Even with, like, clumps in it?
-Wait. Clumps.

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:41.067
No, the clumps
make it delicious.

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:45.300
And when it says cook
for 28 minutes, cook for 23.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.634
-Julia Child, right here.

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:47.968
-Wait. When it comes out
of the oven, y'all --

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:49.534
And when I ice it,
people are like,

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:51.200
"Is that the cake
your daughter made?"

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.400
I'm like,
"No, that's the cake I made!"

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.534
But it is -- It's a --

00:02:55.534 --> 00:02:57.701
-"My daughter did not make it.
I made it."

00:02:57.701 --> 00:03:00.467
-During COVID, my kids don't
know that birthdays are a thing.

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:02.167
They don't know
that you have big parties.

00:03:02.167 --> 00:03:05.167
They think that you sit
at the house, you have a cake,

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:07.033
and you FaceTime,
you know, with the --

00:03:07.033 --> 00:03:09.167
That's what they think
birthdays are. I'm pumped.

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:10.701
-That is amazing. That's right.
They're that young.

00:03:10.701 --> 00:03:12.133
-I am totally pumped.
-Yeah.

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:15.133
I -- My parents started
this silly tradition

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:17.501
of always getting me
an ice-cream cake from Carvel.

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:20.701
I loved it. Thank you, Mom.
Thank you, Dad. But, yeah, no.

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:23.000
There was a couple years
where they forgot,

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.334
and it's heartbreaking.

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:25.534
-It's like -- Yeah.
-Yeah, and then they go,

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:26.767
"Where are we going to get
an ice-cream cake?

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:28.400
Poor Jimmy's, you know --

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.567
Again, he's 17.
He's 17 years old.

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:34.267
Yeah, but I remember once,
my grandma, they put it in --

00:03:34.267 --> 00:03:37.000
My grandma just left it out.
She just thought it was a cake.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.968
And by the time I was
blowing out the candles,

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:40.501
it was just soup
all over the thing.

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:43.667
It was just a total disaster.

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:45.133
Well, there's a couple things
that happened this year

00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:46.534
that I wanted
to talk to you about.

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:48.033
-Okay.
-I'm glad the family is good.

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:50.167
But you started off the new year

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:52.767
with a little con-troversy,
as they say.

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.200
Yeah. Hoda.
-Me?

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.968
-Yeah. A little con-troversy.
-Con-troversy?

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:59.501
-Yeah, con-troversy.
Because -- A little controversy.

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:01.167
-There's no controversy.
-There is.

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:03.367
-No, there's not. Okay, go on.
Tell the thing.

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:05.567
-I think you're going to
bring up what I think

00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:06.767
needs to be addressed.

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:08.167
-Thank you. The polar plunge.

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:10.701
-Thank you for having the
courage to speak truth to power.

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:12.767
-Wow. Finally.
-Thank you.

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:15.133
-Everyone knows what
a polar plunge is, right?

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:17.567
This thing, you go in the
freezing-cold lake or water,

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:19.868
and you go in and you go --
-Can I set the stage?

00:04:19.868 --> 00:04:22.300
It was 16 degrees.
It was freezing.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:25.334
Jenna and I were
in bathing suits, okay?

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:26.834
-That's polar plunge.

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:29.801
-Wait. We had to go
into the ocean. Okay?

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:31.267
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:04:31.267 --> 00:04:33.968
-Don't let her reframe --
-That's the polar plunge.

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:35.334
Everyone agrees with you.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:37.868
Everyone, get your clickers out.
Do you agree?

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:41.167
[ Laughter ]
No, don't get your clickers out.

00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:42.934
But then I have video of you
doing the plunge.

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:44.901
Here's Hoda
doing the polar plunge.

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:46.334
-Yeah.
-You take a look.

00:04:46.334 --> 00:04:48.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:52.434
-Come on, Hoda! Plunge!

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:56.267
-Yes.

00:04:56.267 --> 00:04:57.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:57.634 --> 00:05:00.367
-Don't clap.
-Yes.

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:02.133
-They're clapping,
but I don't know --

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:04.000
Can we see that in slow motion?

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.834
The part that's
very controversial?

00:05:06.834 --> 00:05:09.100
That's not the plu--
-Look at Jenna!

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.834
-Jenna is diving right in.

00:05:10.834 --> 00:05:12.200
Jenna. You --
-No.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.534
-You went with a --
You went with like --

00:05:14.534 --> 00:05:17.334
-You dipped your head in the way
you dip a chip in guacamole.

00:05:17.334 --> 00:05:19.534
-You did a "Sports Illustrated"
Swimsuit Edition.

00:05:19.534 --> 00:05:21.434
You're like, "Wait. Hi.

00:05:21.434 --> 00:05:23.434
Oh, am I in the polar plunge?
Sorry."

00:05:23.434 --> 00:05:25.968
-That was not a polar plunge.
That was a polar dip.

00:05:25.968 --> 00:05:28.133
-I'm gonna ask your audience.

00:05:28.133 --> 00:05:31.400
Ladies and gentlemen,
did I do a polar plunge?

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:32.601
[ Audience shouting, "No!" ]

00:05:32.601 --> 00:05:34.801
Wait! What?!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.467
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:38.467
Wait. No?

00:05:38.467 --> 00:05:40.734
-Wow! A mixed reaction.

00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:42.834
-Oh! I thought I could
hype the crowd.

00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:45.300
-No, but you can ask --
But did she look cool doing it?

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.968
-Yeah.
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:46.968 --> 00:05:48.868
-Yeah, there you go.
You looked really cool.

00:05:48.868 --> 00:05:51.334
I did -- I got to be honest.
I did a polar plunge.

00:05:51.334 --> 00:05:52.701
-You did? All the way in?
-Yeah.

00:05:52.701 --> 00:05:54.267
Lake Michigan.
I went all the way in.

00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:55.901
-Oh, my God.
-And everything freezes.

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:58.200
It was ridiculous.
It was in Chicago.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:01.200
And I got out,
and I heard bagpipes and --

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.868
[ Laughter ]
-You thought you died.

00:06:02.868 --> 00:06:04.934
-That's what Irish people hear
when they die.

00:06:04.934 --> 00:06:08.067
And I go -- I thought
I floated away in Lake Michigan.

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:10.167
I go, "This is --"
But I survived.

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:12.634
There were just
actual bagpipes playing.

00:06:12.634 --> 00:06:13.834
-Oh, you did it in a suit?

00:06:13.834 --> 00:06:16.000
-Yeah, there actually
was bagpipers. Yeah.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.601
-Oh, my gosh.
-You know what?

00:06:17.601 --> 00:06:19.934
That's how you know
he actually did the plunge.

00:06:19.934 --> 00:06:22.801
-It was a nightmare.
It was a nightmare.

00:06:22.801 --> 00:06:25.601
Guys, I want to talk to you
about this big hall of fame.

00:06:25.601 --> 00:06:27.434
This is a giant honor
for you guys.

00:06:27.434 --> 00:06:28.801
Are you freaking out?

00:06:28.801 --> 00:06:30.234
-The Broadcasting &amp; Cable
Hall of Fame?

00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:31.934
-Yeah.
-I mean, yeah.

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:33.734
We were like --
We basically feel like it --

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:34.968
That's how you know you're old.

00:06:34.968 --> 00:06:36.267
You're just like, "Okay."
-No, no.

00:06:36.267 --> 00:06:37.767
That's how you know
that you're a legend.

00:06:37.767 --> 00:06:39.534
-There's no young people
in the hall of fame.

00:06:39.534 --> 00:06:41.267
-Now there are two.
There's about to be two.

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:42.834
Let's talk about it
when we come back.

00:06:42.834 --> 00:06:45.133
Savannah Guthrie, Hoda Kotb.
Come on back, everybody.

